	<p><strong>Last Updated: 14 October 2026</strong></p>
	<h2>1. Introduction</h2>
	<p>CheckClimate Africa (“CheckClimate Africa”, “we”, “our”, or “us”) is committed to protecting your privacy and handling your personal information responsibly.</p>
	<p>We are a climate information and media platform dedicated to disseminating accurate, evidence-based climate information, promoting climate awareness, and addressing climate misinformation across Africa.</p>
	<p>This Privacy Policy explains how we collect, use, store, protect, and disclose personal information when you visit <a href="/"><strong>https://checkclimate.africa/</strong></a>, contact our team, submit information for fact-checking, or otherwise interact with our website.</p>
	<p>By using our website, you acknowledge that you have read this Privacy Policy. Where applicable law requires consent for specific data-processing activities, we will seek that consent separately.</p>
	<h2>2. Information We Collect</h2>
	<p>The personal information we collect depends on how you interact with our website.</p>
	<h3>2.1 Information You Provide to Us</h3>
	<p>We may collect personal information that you voluntarily provide, including:</p>
	<ul>
		<li><strong>Contact information:</strong> Your name, email address, telephone number, or organisation, where provided.</li>
		<li><strong>Enquiries and correspondence:</strong> Information contained in messages, questions, feedback, complaints, or requests sent to us.</li>
		<li><strong>Fact-checking submissions:</strong> Climate-related claims, articles, images, videos, links, documents, and explanations you submit for verification. These submissions may contain personal information about you or other individuals.</li>
		<li><strong>Newsletter subscriptions:</strong> Your name and email address, if you choose to subscribe to our newsletter or other updates.</li>
		<li><strong>Professional and programme information:</strong> Information you provide when expressing interest in our training programmes, events, partnerships, or other activities.</li>
	</ul>
	<p>Please avoid including sensitive personal information that is not necessary for your enquiry or submission.</p>
	<h3>2.2 Information Collected Automatically</h3>
	<p>When you visit our website, certain technical information may be collected automatically by our website infrastructure or service providers. Depending on the services enabled, this may include:</p>
	<ul>
		<li>Internet Protocol (IP) address.</li>
		<li>Browser type and version.</li>
		<li>Device and operating system information.</li>
		<li>Pages visited and the date and time of access.</li>
		<li>Referring websites and general website navigation information.</li>
		<li>Technical logs relating to website performance, errors, and security.</li>
	</ul>
	<p>We use this information, where applicable, to maintain the website, understand how visitors use our content, troubleshoot technical problems, and protect the website against misuse.</p>
	<h3>2.3 Cookies and Similar Technologies</h3>
	<p>Our website or its service providers may use cookies and similar technologies to support website functionality, remember preferences, understand website traffic, and improve the user experience.</p>
	<p>Cookies are small files stored on your device by a website.</p>
	<p>Depending on the technologies in use, cookies may include:</p>
	<ul>
		<li><strong>Essential cookies:</strong> Necessary for basic website functionality, security, or the proper operation of certain features.</li>
		<li><strong>Analytics cookies:</strong> Used to understand visitor behaviour and measure website performance.</li>
		<li><strong>Preference cookies:</strong> Used to remember certain settings or preferences.</li>
	</ul>
	<p>You can manage cookies through your browser settings. Disabling certain cookies may affect the functionality of parts of the website.</p>
	<p>Where required by applicable law, we will obtain consent before using non-essential cookies or similar technologies.</p>
	<h2>3. How We Use Your Information</h2>
	<p>We may use personal information for the following purposes:</p>
	<ol>
		<li><strong>Operating our website:</strong> To provide access to our climate news, research, fact-checks, analysis, and other published content.</li>
		<li><strong>Responding to enquiries:</strong> To answer questions, feedback, complaints, and requests submitted through our contact channels.</li>
		<li><strong>Climate fact-checking:</strong> To review claims and supporting materials submitted to us, communicate with relevant sources, and investigate potential climate misinformation.</li>
		<li><strong>Editorial and research activities:</strong> To verify information, seek clarification, contact relevant sources, and support responsible climate reporting.</li>
		<li><strong>Communications:</strong> To send newsletters, updates, or information about our activities where you have subscribed or where another lawful basis applies.</li>
		<li><strong>Website improvement:</strong> To understand readership patterns, improve navigation, evaluate content performance, and enhance accessibility.</li>
		<li><strong>Security and fraud prevention:</strong> To detect suspicious activity, prevent unauthorised access, and protect our systems and users.</li>
		<li><strong>Legal compliance:</strong> To comply with applicable laws, lawful requests, and other legitimate legal obligations.</li>
	</ol>
	<p>We will not use your personal information for purposes that are incompatible with the reasons for which it was collected without an appropriate lawful basis.</p>
	<h2>4. Legal Basis for Processing</h2>
	<p>Where applicable, we process personal information on one or more lawful grounds, including:</p>
	<ul>
		<li>Your consent.</li>
		<li>The need to take steps you request or fulfil an agreement with you.</li>
		<li>Our legitimate interests in operating the website, maintaining security, responding to enquiries, and carrying out responsible editorial and fact-checking activities, provided those interests do not override your rights.</li>
		<li>Compliance with legal obligations.</li>
		<li>Other lawful grounds recognised by applicable data protection legislation.</li>
	</ul>
	<p>Where we rely on consent, you may withdraw it at any time. Withdrawal does not affect the lawfulness of processing carried out before your consent was withdrawn.</p>
	<h2>5. Climate Fact-Checking and Editorial Privacy</h2>
	<p>CheckClimate Africa may receive information from members of the public, researchers, journalists, organisations, and other sources to investigate climate-related claims and potential misinformation.</p>
	<p>We handle such submissions with appropriate care and use them for editorial verification, research, and related purposes.</p>
	<p>Submitting information does not automatically guarantee that it will be published, investigated, or used in a published fact-check.</p>
	<p>We may contact you to clarify a submission or request additional information. Where appropriate, we may also contact other relevant sources to verify the information provided.</p>
	<p><strong>Please note:</strong> We cannot guarantee absolute confidentiality for every submission. Information may need to be shared with authorised editorial personnel, relevant service providers, or other parties where necessary for verification, publication, security, or compliance with the law.</p>
	<p>We take reasonable steps to avoid unnecessarily disclosing the identity or personal information of individuals who submit information to us. However, information you voluntarily provide may identify you, and material included in a public submission may be published where editorially justified and legally permissible.</p>
	<p>If you are submitting sensitive information or wish to discuss confidentiality arrangements, please contact us before sharing it.</p>
	<h2>6. When We Share Personal Information</h2>
	<p>We do not sell your personal information to third parties.</p>
	<p>We may share personal information in the following circumstances:</p>
	<h3>6.1 Service Providers</h3>
	<p>We may use third-party providers for website hosting, maintenance, security, email delivery, analytics, and other operational services.</p>
	<p>These providers may process personal information on our behalf where necessary to provide their services. Where appropriate, we take reasonable steps to ensure that they protect the information and use it only for authorised purposes.</p>
	<h3>6.2 Editorial Verification</h3>
	<p>Where necessary for a fact-check or investigation, we may share relevant information with editors, researchers, subject-matter experts, or other sources involved in verifying a claim.</p>
	<p>We aim to limit such sharing to information reasonably necessary for the relevant purpose.</p>
	<h3>6.3 Legal and Regulatory Requirements</h3>
	<p>We may disclose personal information where required or permitted by law, court order, or a valid request from an authorised public authority, or where disclosure is reasonably necessary to protect our legal rights or prevent serious harm.</p>
	<h3>6.4 Organisational Changes</h3>
	<p>If our operations undergo a merger, restructuring, transfer, or similar organisational change, personal information may be transferred where legally permitted and subject to appropriate safeguards.</p>
	<h2>7. Third-Party Websites and Services</h2>
	<p>Our website may contain links to external websites, research publications, social media platforms, videos, and other third-party resources.</p>
	<p>These external websites operate independently and have their own privacy policies and data-handling practices. We do not control how they collect or use personal information.</p>
	<p>When you follow an external link, we encourage you to review the privacy policy of the relevant website or service before providing personal information.</p>
	<p>This Privacy Policy applies only to CheckClimate Africa&#39;s website and the personal information we process within its scope.</p>
	<h2>8. International Data Transfers</h2>
	<p>Some of our service providers may store or process information outside Nigeria or outside the country in which you reside.</p>
	<p>Where personal information is transferred across borders, we will take appropriate steps to ensure that the transfer complies with applicable data protection laws and that suitable safeguards are in place.</p>
	<h2>9. How We Protect Your Information</h2>
	<p>We take reasonable technical, organisational, and administrative measures to protect personal information against unauthorised access, disclosure, alteration, loss, or misuse.</p>
	<p>These measures may include access restrictions, appropriate security controls, system monitoring, and secure handling of information by authorised personnel and service providers.</p>
	<p>However, no website, internet transmission, or electronic storage system can be guaranteed to be completely secure. We therefore cannot promise absolute security.</p>
	<p>If a personal data breach occurs, we will take appropriate steps in accordance with applicable legal requirements.</p>
	<h2>10. How Long We Retain Your Information</h2>
	<p>We retain personal information only for as long as reasonably necessary to fulfil the purposes described in this Privacy Policy, meet legal obligations, resolve disputes, maintain appropriate records, and protect our legitimate interests.</p>
	<p>Retention periods may vary depending on the type of information and the purpose for which it was collected.</p>
	<p>For example:</p>
	<ul>
		<li><strong>Enquiries and correspondence:</strong> Retained for as long as needed to respond and maintain relevant records.</li>
		<li><strong>Fact-checking submissions:</strong> Retained for the duration reasonably necessary for editorial review, verification, documentation, and any applicable legal or archival requirements.</li>
		<li><strong>Newsletter information:</strong> Retained while you remain subscribed, unless a longer retention period is required by law or necessary to maintain suppression records for unsubscribe requests.</li>
		<li><strong>Technical and analytics information:</strong> Retained according to operational needs and the applicable retention settings of our service providers.</li>
	</ul>
	<p>When personal information is no longer required, we will take reasonable steps to delete it or anonymise it, subject to applicable legal requirements.</p>
	<h2>11. Your Privacy Rights</h2>
	<p>Subject to applicable law, you may have the right to:</p>
	<ul>
		<li><strong>Access</strong> personal information we hold about you.</li>
		<li><strong>Request correction</strong> of inaccurate or incomplete information.</li>
		<li><strong>Request deletion</strong> of personal information where the law permits.</li>
		<li><strong>Object to or request restriction of processing</strong> in circumstances recognised by law.</li>
		<li><strong>Withdraw consent</strong> where processing is based on consent.</li>
		<li><strong>Request a copy or transfer</strong> of your personal information where applicable.</li>
		<li><strong>Lodge a complaint</strong> with the relevant data protection authority.</li>
	</ul>
	<p>These rights are subject to applicable legal conditions and exceptions. For example, we may need to retain certain information to comply with the law or protect legitimate editorial, legal, or security interests.</p>
	<p>To exercise a privacy right, please contact us using the details in Section 15. We may need to verify your identity before responding to your request.</p>
	<p>We will handle requests within the timeframes required by applicable law.</p>
	<h2>12. Children&#39;s Privacy</h2>
	<p>Our website publishes public-interest climate information and may be accessed by people of different ages.</p>
	<p>We do not knowingly collect personal information from children where doing so would violate applicable data protection laws. Where information about a child is collected, we will handle it in accordance with applicable legal requirements and appropriate safeguards.</p>
	<p>If you believe that a child has provided personal information to us inappropriately, please contact us so that we can review the situation and take appropriate action.</p>
	<h2>13. Email Communications and Newsletters</h2>
	<p>If we offer a newsletter or email subscription service, we may use the contact information you provide to send the updates you request.</p>
	<p>You may unsubscribe from marketing or newsletter communications at any time by using the unsubscribe instructions included in the message, where available, or by contacting us directly.</p>
	<p>Unsubscribing from a newsletter will not necessarily prevent us from sending essential responses to enquiries you have made or other communications we are legally permitted or required to send.</p>
	<h2>14. Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>
	<p>We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time to reflect changes in our website, editorial activities, technology, legal obligations, or data-handling practices.</p>
	<p>When we make changes, we will update the “Last Updated” date at the top of this page. Where required by law, we will provide additional notice or seek consent for material changes.</p>
	<p>We encourage you to review this page periodically to stay informed about how we protect your personal information.</p>
	<h2>15. Contact Us</h2>
	<p>If you have questions about this Privacy Policy, wish to exercise your privacy rights, or have a concern about how your personal information is handled, please contact us:</p>
	<p><strong>Organisation:</strong> CheckClimate Africa</p>
	<p><strong>Website:</strong> <a href="/">https://checkclimate.africa/</a></p>
	<p><strong>Email:</strong> <a href="mailto:CheckClimateAfrica@gmail.com">CheckClimateAfrica@gmail.com</a></p>
	<p>Please include “Privacy Request” in the subject line of your email to help us direct your enquiry to the appropriate person.</p>
	<h2>16. Applicable Data Protection Law</h2>
	<p>CheckClimate Africa aims to handle personal information in accordance with applicable data protection laws, including the Nigeria Data Protection Act 2023, where applicable.</p>
	<p>Nothing in this Privacy Policy is intended to exclude or limit any rights you may have under applicable law.</p>
</StaticPage>
